Since the no-arg `onUpdateCheckpointDirection()` method was created in candidate_02 and never touched again by any subsequent candidate until it was finally corrected by the fix, candidate_02 is the commit that introduced (and left in place) the exact code that later became incompatible with the interface, ultimately causing the build error. It is the earliest and only candidate that established this specific piece of problematic code.

